web: let an embedder show the workbench's menu bar natively

The desktop workbench gives its menu bar to Electron's main process as data (NativeMenubarControl -> IMenubarData), and the main
process shows it in the operating system's menu bar with the keybindings as accelerators. The web workbench always draws its own
menu bar in the page. An embedder that hosts the web workbench in a desktop shell (here the vmapp loader, which can show an app's
menus in the Mac menu bar) has no way to take the menu bar out of the page.

This adds EmbedderMenubarControl: when the embedding page provides `nativeMenubar` among its non-JSON embedder options
(globalThis.vscodeWebEmbedderOptions, the same global as patch 0001), the title bar creates it instead of the in-page menu bar. It
builds exactly the data NativeMenubarControl builds, from the same menus and keybindings, gives it to the embedder's update(), and
runs the command (or opens the Open Recent entry) the embedder reports with onDidRun(). Without that option nothing changes.

